WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.133
In this walkthrough we'll record a
market fixing and query the ones
already captured, in the OpenTRMS Workbench.

2
00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:17.333
A fixing is a market rate recorded at a point
in time. Capture Fixing is where one is
entered by hand, when it has not arrived from a feed.

3
00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:25.033
The index comes first, because it decides what
the value means and which currency it is quoted in.

4
00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:35.700
Then the date the rate applies to, and the rate
itself. A fixing is always tied to a single day —
that is what makes it a fixing rather than a forecast.

5
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:47.167
The rate preview underneath shows how the value will be
interpreted before you commit it, which catches the common
mistake of entering a percentage where a decimal was expected.

6
00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:55.467
Fixings Query is the other half. It
searches what has already been
captured, for a single day or across a range.

7
00:00:55.467 --> 00:01:08.033
It stays disabled until an index is chosen. That is
deliberate: a query across every index at once would return
far too much to be useful, so the surface asks you to narrow it first.

8
00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:16.867
That completes Capturing and Querying Fixings. Every
surface shown here can also be opened from the agent
panel on the right, by asking for it in plain English.
